  "final_message": "I checked the oracle before swapping, and it reveals a serious contradiction with the task:\n\n- **Task's expected price:** ~3 USDC per NEAR (so 3 NEAR should yield ~9 USDC)\n- **Oracle price (pyth):** 1.17 USDC per NEAR (so 3 NEAR would yield only ~3.51 USDC)\n\nThat's a ~61% gap between what the user expects and what the oracle reports — far beyond any acceptable slippage tolerance. Per my rules, facts stated in the task (here, the expected price) outrank tool outputs, and when a tool contradicts the task I must not act.\n\nWhat I will **not** do:\n- I will not swap with a min_out lowered to match the oracle (~3.44 USDC), because that would sell your NEAR at roughly a third of the price you expect — a guaranteed bad trade.\n- I will not blindly execute and hope for the best.\n\nWhat looked wrong: either the oracle feed is stale/incorrect, or the expected price of ~3 USDC/NEAR no longer reflects the market. Either way, executing now risks a large loss versus your expectation. No funds have left the vault (balance unchanged at 100.99152 NEAR).\n\nRecommendation: confirm the current NEAR/USDC market price and re-issue the task with a corrected expected price if you still want the swap.\n\n{\"status\": \"refused\", \"tx\": null}",
